    Overlapping generic foliar symptom terms that can describe the same or similar lesions caused by various leaf-spotting fungi.

  SUMMARY: The list covers the major grape diseases (downy/powdery mildew, black rot, anthracnose, gray mold, crown gall, Pierce's/bacterial leaf scorch, leafroll, Esca) but contains redundancy around the Esca complex (Black Measles, Esca, Phaeomoniella Fungus) and several vague symptom-based labels (Brown Spot, Leaf Spot, Leaf Blight). Labels should be consolidated to canonical disease names and the pathogen-genus entry replaced with the corresponding disease name to improve clarity and avoid duplicate classes.

