  ~ SIMILAR: Artist S Conk | Red-Belted Fungus | White Heartwood Rot
    All describe wood-decay fungi or the resulting heart/white rot of poplar trunks rather than distinct named diseases.

  SUMMARY: Most entries represent genuine poplar diseases (Hypoxylon canker, Cytospora canker, Septoria, bronze leaf, bacterial wetwood, Armillaria, powdery mildew, ink spot, shepherd's crook). Several labels are vague, name organisms/fruiting bodies (Artist's conk, Red-belted fungus, Morel) or broad decay categories (white heartwood rot, sooty mold) rather than specific diseases, and there is clear duplication between the two Hypoxylon canker entries. Cleanup should remove Morel, consolidate the Hypoxylon duplicates, and replace vague labels like 'Leaf Spot' and 'Black Rot' with specific pathogen-based disease names.

