  SUMMARY: The potato list contains a solid core of real potato diseases (late blight, early blight, common scab, powdery scab, black scurf/Rhizoctonia, bacterial soft rot, PVY, TRV, TSWV) but is heavily contaminated with sweetpotato diseases (Scurf, Streptomyces Soil Rot, Java Black Rot, Diaporthe destruens, Fusarium Root Rot Of Sweetpotato, SPFMV) and diseases of unrelated crops (Apple Scab, White Rust). Several entries are pathogen genus/species names rather than diseases (Geotrichum Fungi, Penicillium Fungi, Fusarium Lateritium Nees, Globisporangium Ultimum), and there are duplicates and malformed multi-disease labels (Fusarium Wilt/Wilts, Bacteria Wilt And Soft Rot). Overall label quality is poor and requires deduplication, removal of non-potato hosts, and conversion of pathogen names into proper disease names.

