    ?  Parastagonospora Nodorum: Names the pathogen instead of the disease (Stagonospora nodorum blotch / glume blotch).
    ?  Penicillium Fungi: Penicillium is mainly a post-harvest grain storage mold, not a field disease of wheat; label names a fungal genus.
    ?  Root Rot: Generic label; wheat root rots are caused by many pathogens (Fusarium, Pythium, Rhizoctonia, Gaeumannomyces).
    ?  Rust: Vague; wheat has three distinct rust diseases (stem, leaf, stripe) that should be specified.
    ?  Septoria Leaf Spot And Cankers: Septoria leaf spot occurs in wheat but 'cankers' are not a feature of Septoria on wheat; label appears conflated with tree Septoria diseases.
    ?  Smut: Generic; wheat smuts include loose smut, flag smut, and the bunts, which should be specified.
    ?  Sooty Mold: Sooty molds on wheat heads (sooty head molds by Alternaria, Cladosporium, etc.) are minor saprophytic issues, not primary diseases.
    ?  Zymoseptoria Tritici: Names the pathogen rather than the disease (Septoria tritici blotch).

  ~ SIMILAR: Bacterial Leaf Streak Black Chaff | Bacterial Streak | Leaf Streakblack Chaff
    All three refer to bacterial leaf streak / black chaff caused by Xanthomonas translucens.

  ~ SIMILAR: Barley Yellow Dwarf Virus | Wheat Barley Yellow Dwarf
    Both name the same BYDV disease on wheat.

  ~ SIMILAR: Powdery Mildew | Blumeria Graminis F
    Pathogen-name label for the same disease (powdery mildew).

  ~ SIMILAR: Septoria Leaf Blotch | Zymoseptoria Tritici
    Same disease (Septoria tritici blotch) named by disease vs. pathogen.

  ~ SIMILAR: Glume Blotch | Parastagonospora Nodorum
    Same disease (Stagonospora nodorum / glume blotch) named by disease vs. pathogen.

  ~ SIMILAR: Head Scab | Fusarium Disease | Fusarium Graminearum Schwabe
    All overlap with Fusarium head blight (head scab) caused by F. graminearum.

  ~ SIMILAR: Cephalosporium Stripe | Wheat Cephalosporium Stripe
    Identical disease, duplicate entry.

  ~ SIMILAR: Stem Rust | Wheat Stem Rust
    Same disease, duplicate entry.

  ~ SIMILAR: Stripe Rust | Wheat Stripe Rust
    Same disease, duplicate entry.

  ~ SIMILAR: Rust | Wheat Leaf Rust | Wheat Stem Rust | Wheat Stripe Rust | Stem Rust | Stripe Rust
    Generic 'Rust' subsumes the three specific wheat rusts also listed separately.

  ~ SIMILAR: Common Bunt | Dwarf Bunt | Karnal Bunt | Wheat Bunt
    'Wheat Bunt' is a generic umbrella for the specific bunt diseases also listed.

  ~ SIMILAR: Smut | Loose Smut | Common Bunt | Dwarf Bunt | Karnal Bunt
    Generic 'Smut' overlaps with the specific smut/bunt diseases listed.

  ~ SIMILAR: Eyespot | Sharp Eyespot | Foot Rot
    All are stem-base diseases of wheat with overlapping symptoms and partly overlapping causal agents.

  ~ SIMILAR: Root Rot | Take-All Root Rot | Rhizoctonia Damping-Off | Pythium Diseases | Phytophthora Root And Crown Rots
    Generic 'Root Rot' overlaps with the specific root-rot diseases listed.

  ~ SIMILAR: Alternaria Blight | Alternaria Black Molds Stem Cankers
    Both invoke Alternaria on wheat; the second label is a garbled/conflated variant.

  SUMMARY: The list captures most of the major wheat diseases (rusts, bunts/smuts, Fusarium head blight, Septoria/Stagonospora blotches, tan spot, powdery mildew, BYDV, WSMV, take-all, eyespot, Cephalosporium stripe) but is noisy. Several entries duplicate one another (rusts, bunts, Cephalosporium stripe, bacterial streak/black chaff) or name pathogens instead of diseases (Blumeria graminis, Zymoseptoria tritici, Parastagonospora nodorum, Fusarium graminearum). A few entries are incorrect for wheat (Phytophthora root/crown rots, Fusarium wilts, the bean/stone-fruit bacterial entry, 'Resistance Phenotype') and several are overly generic (Rust, Smut, Leaf Spot, Root Rot, Fusarium Disease) and should be resolved to specific diseases.

