  SUMMARY: The list mixes well-established zinnia diseases (Alternaria blight, powdery mildew, TSWV) with vague or pathogen-named entries that are not proper disease labels. 'Berkeleyomyces basicola' and 'Cladosporium fungi' should be reframed as diseases (black root rot, Cladosporium leaf spot), and 'Flower Blights' is too generic and overlaps with Alternaria blight. Overall label quality is inconsistent and would benefit from standardization to disease names.

